doc/figures/ - TikZ diagrams
============================

Standalone TikZ pictures, one per file, \input inside a figure environment in
the section that uses them. They share the node/edge styles and colour palette
defined in ../config/tikz.tex and ../config/colors.tex, so they render as one
visual system.

    pe.tex         processing-element datapath (muxes, ALU, register, config)
    array.tex      the 4x4 mesh + north/west edge operand injection
    fsm.tex        the control finite-state machine (ID/CFG/WR/RUN/RD/RST)
    systolic.tex   weight-stationary matrix-vector space-time skew
    stack.tex      the layered host/device software stack

Style keys (see ../config/tikz.tex): blk, alu, reg, mux, pe, st, wire, lbl.
Reuse them instead of hard-coding colours so a palette change propagates
everywhere at once.
